.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt NOVI-AGENT-SERVE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm novi-agent-serve
.Nd handle one request on the agent socket
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the per-connection handler
.Nm s6-ipcserver
runs for the
.Va services.novi-agentd
service.
It reads one line from standard input, checks that it is a request,
and execs
.Xr novi-agent 1 .
It is not run by hand.
.Pp
The point of the service is that the privilege moves: a large
untrusted program runs as nobody in particular, and a small reviewed
one holds root.
What may be done is unchanged \(em
.Va agent.allow
still decides that.
.Ss The handler holds no policy
.Nm
rejects only a request that is
.Em not a request :
no credentials, no line, over 512 bytes, or control characters.
Every decision about what a verb may do lives in
.Xr novi-agent 1 .
.Pp
That is not tidiness.
The socket refusal for
.Cm wifi.join
was written here first, where it worked and left no trace: the
handler exits before
.Xr novi-agent 1
runs, and
.Xr novi-agent 1
is the only thing that writes the audit log \(em so the attempt most
worth recording was the one that vanished.
.Ss Identity comes from the kernel
The peer's uid arrives through
.Dv SO_PEERCRED
.Pf ( Nm s6-ipcserver Fl p ) ,
never from the request, and reaches the audit log as
.Ev NOVI_AGENT_PEER_UID .
.Nm id Fl u
would have recorded root for every request whoever made it, which is
the one question an audit log exists to answer, with a single wrong
answer.
A
.Va via
field separates
.Dq root at a shell
from
.Dq root through the socket ,
which a uid cannot.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width "NOVI_AGENT_PEER_UID" -compact
.It Ev IPCREMOTEEUID
Set by
.Nm s6-ipcserver Fl p .
.It Ev NOVI_AGENT_PEER_UID
.It Ev NOVI_AGENT_VIA
Passed to
.Xr novi-agent 1 .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/run/novi/agent/sock" -compact
.It Pa /run/novi/agent
Mode 2750,
.Sy root:agent .
The setgid bit is the whole feature:
.Nm s6-ipcserver
binds as root, so without it the socket is created
.Sy root:root
and mode 0660 gives the
.Sy agent
group nothing.
.It Pa /run/novi/agent/sock
The socket.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr novi-agent 1 ,
.Xr system.conf 5
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC 0032.
.Sh CAVEATS
A process reaching the socket must actually
.Em carry
the
.Sy agent
group.
BusyBox
.Nm setuidgid
drops supplementary groups and is denied;
.Nm s6-setuidgid
keeps them and connects.
That constrains whatever launches an agent here, not just how it was
tested.
